.SH "DDC TAB-DUMP FORMAT"
.IX Header "DDC TAB-DUMP FORMAT"
This manual page describes the output format produced by the \f(CW\*(C`ddc_dump\*(C'\fR
program using the \f(CW\*(C`\-\-full \-\-tabs\*(C'\fR (\f(CW\*(C`\-f \-t\*(C'\fR) option(s).  When running in
this mode, the \f(CW\*(C`\-\-output DIR\*(C'\fR option specifies the directory \f(CW\*(C`DIR\*(C'\fR to which file(s)
are to be written.  One output file \fI\s-1DIR/FID\s0.tabs\fR is created in the specified directory
for each document represented in the index, where \f(CW\*(C`FID\*(C'\fR is the logical index-number
of the corresponding document, starting from zero.  The remainder of this document
describes the format of the \fI\s-1DIR/FID\s0.tabs\fR file(s).
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\& ##=====================================================================
\& ## File Format
\& 
\& TABDUMP ::= HEADER BODY
\& 
\& ##=====================================================================
\& ## Header Section
\& 
\& HEADER ::= (TOKRANGE | META | PAGE | BREAK | INDEX)*
\& 
\& TOKRANGE    ::= TOKID_BEGIN TOKID_END
\& TOKID_BEGIN ::= "%%$DDC:tokid.begin=" TOKID "\en"
\& TOKID_END   ::= "%%$DDC:tokid.end=" TOKID "\en"
\& 
\& META  ::= "%%$DDC.meta." META_NAME . "=" META_VALUE "\en"
\& 
\& PAGE  ::= "%%$DDC:PAGE=" PAGENO "\en"
\& BREAK ::= "%%$DDC:BREAK." BREAK_NAME "[" BREAK_ID "]=" TOKID "\en"
\& 
\& INDEX ::= "%%$DDC:index[" INDEX_ID "]=" INDEX_LONG " " INDEX_SHORT "\en"
\& 
\& ##=====================================================================
\& ## Body Section
\& 
\& BODY ::= (TOKEN | BREAK | EOS)*
\& 
\& TOKEN ::= INDEX_VAL ("\et" INDEX_VAL)* "\en"
\& EOS   ::= "\en"
\& 
\& ##=====================================================================
\& ## Lexical Content
\& 
\& TOKID       ::= {integer}   /* running counter of indexed token positions */
\& META_NAME   ::= {string}    /* bibliographic metadata attribute name */
\& META_VALUE  ::= {string}    /* bibliographic metadata attribute value */
\& PAGENO      ::= {integer}   /* internal page counter */
\& BREAK_NAME  ::= {string}    /* short break\-names are used */
\& INDEX_ID    ::= {integer}   /* position of indexed attribute\-value in token\-lines */
\& INDEX_LONG  ::= {string}    /* long token\-level index name */
\& INDEX_SHORT ::= {string}    /* short token\-level index name */
\& INDEX_VAL   ::= {string}    /* value of indexed attribute */
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
.SS "File Format"
.IX Subsection "File Format"
.Vb 1
\& TABDUMP ::= HEADER BODY
.Ve
.PP
\&\s-1DDC\s0 tab-dump files are comprised of a header section
followed by a body section; see
\&\*(L"Header Section\*(R" and \*(L"Body Section\*(R" for details.
.SS "Header Section"
.IX Subsection "Header Section"
.Vb 1
\& HEADER ::= (TOKRANGE | META | BREAK | INDEX)*
.Ve
.PP
\&\s-1DDC\s0 tab-dump files begin with a simple header section.
Header data, like all non-token data begins with the string
\&\f(CW%%$DDC\fR to make it easy to identify.
The header section may contain the following information:
.PP
\fIToken Range\fR
.IX Subsection "Token Range"
.PP
.Vb 3
\& TOKRANGE    ::= TOKID_BEGIN TOKID_END
\& TOKID_BEGIN ::= "%%$DDC:tokid.begin=" TOKID "\en"
\& TOKID_END   ::= "%%$DDC:tokid.end=" TOKID "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Reports the range of DDC-internal token-IDs covered by the current document.
.PP
\fIBibliographic Metadata\fR
.IX Subsection "Bibliographic Metadata"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& META  ::= "%%$DDC.meta." META_NAME . "=" META_VALUE "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Reports the value of the bibliographic metadata attribute \f(CW\*(C`META_NAME\*(C'\fR
as \f(CW\*(C`META_VALUE\*(C'\fR.  Built-in metadata fields are reported with a trailing
underscore for \f(CW\*(C`META_NAME\*(C'\fR:
.PP
.Vb 6
\& "%%$DDC.meta.n_=" DOC_ID "\en"
\& "%%$DDC.meta.file_=" DOC_FILENAME "\en"
\& "%%$DDC.meta.scan_=" BIBL_SCAN "\en"
\& "%%$DDC.meta.orig_=" BIBL_ORIG "\en"
\& "%%$DDC.meta.date_=" BIBL_DATE "\en"
\& "%%$DDC.meta.page_=" BIBL_PAGE "\en"
.Ve
.PP
In streaming TAB-format input mode, the \f(CW\*(C`%%$DDC.meta.file_=\*(C'\fR declaration introduces
a document boundary (a.k.a. \*(L"file break\*(R").
.PP
\fIInitial Page\fR
.IX Subsection "Initial Page"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& PAGE  ::= "%%$DDC:PAGE=" PAGENO "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Reports the position of the first internal page-break in the current document.
.PP
\fIInitial Break Positions\fR
.IX Subsection "Initial Break Positions"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& BREAK ::= "%%$DDC:BREAK." BREAK_NAME "[" BREAK_ID "]" =" TOKID "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Reports the position of the first \*(L"break\*(R" of type \f(CW\*(C`BREAK_NAME\*(C'\fR in the current
document.  \f(CW\*(C`BREAK_NAME\*(C'\fR is the short name of some \*(L"break collection\*(R"
declared with the \*(L"HitBorders\*(R" option in the project option-file (*.opt).
\&\f(CW\*(C`BREAK_ID\*(C'\fR is the index of the break in the underlying break-vector,
or \f(CW\*(C`\-1\*(C'\fR if the break is the corpus-initial break of its type, and \f(CW\*(C`TOKID\*(C'\fR
is the token-ID of the first token in the break.
.PP
\fIToken Index Attribute Positions\fR
.IX Subsection "Token Index Attribute Positions"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& INDEX ::= "%%$DDC:index[" INDEX_ID "]=" INDEX_LONG " " INDEX_SHORT "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Reports that the attributes at position \f(CW\*(C`INDEX_ID\*(C'\fR in TAB-separated token lines
corresponds to the indexed token attribute with long name
\&\f(CW\*(C`INDEX_LONG\*(C'\fR and short name \f(CW\*(C`INDEX_SHORT\*(C'\fR,
as declared by the \*(L"Indices\*(R" option in the project option-file (*.opt).
.SS "Body Section"
.IX Subsection "Body Section"
.Vb 1
\& BODY ::= (TOKEN | PAGE | BREAK | EOS)*
.Ve
.PP
The body section consists of zero or more lines representing the indexed
document content.  Each body line represents either an indexed token (\f(CW\*(C`TOKEN\*(C'\fR),
a default hit-boundary (\f(CW\*(C`EOS\*(C'\fR), or an arbitrary document-internal break (\f(CW\*(C`BREAK\*(C'\fR).
.PP
\fIToken\fR
.IX Subsection "Token"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& TOKEN ::= INDEX_VAL ("\et" INDEX_VAL)* "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Tokens are represented as TAB-separated lists of indexed values.
Position \f(CW\*(C`INDEX_ID\*(C'\fR in the TAB-separated list corresponds to the
index attribute declared for \f(CW\*(C`INDEX_ID\*(C'\fR
in some token index attribute position
from the Header Section.
.PP
\fIDefault Hit-Boundary\fR
.IX Subsection "Default Hit-Boundary"
.PP
.Vb 1
\& EOS   ::= "\en"
.Ve
.PP
Boundaries of the default break-collection are represented as blank lines.
.PP
\fIInteral Pagebreaks\fR
.IX Subsection "Interal Pagebreaks"
.PP
Document-interal page-breaks are represented as for
the Initial Page declaration
in the Header Section.
.PP
\fIInteral Breaks\fR
.IX Subsection "Interal Breaks"
.PP
Document-interal breaks are represented as for
Initial Break Positions
in the Header Section.
.SS "Lexical Content"
.IX Subsection "Lexical Content"
.Vb 9
\& TOKID       ::= {integer}   /* running counter of indexed token positions */
\& META_NAME   ::= {string}    /* bibliographic metadata attribute name */
\& META_VALUE  ::= {string}    /* bibliographic metadata attribute value */
\& PAGENO      ::= {integer}   /* internal page counter */
\& BREAK_NAME  ::= {string}    /* short break\-names are used */
\& INDEX_ID    ::= {integer}   /* position of indexed attribute\-value in token\-lines */
\& INDEX_LONG  ::= {string}    /* long token\-level index name */
\& INDEX_SHORT ::= {string}    /* short token\-level index name */
\& INDEX_VAL   ::= {string}    /* value of indexed attribute */
.Ve
.PP
Integers are represented in decimal notation,
dates are represented as  \f(CW\*(C`YYYY\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`YYYY\-MM\*(C'\fR, or \f(CW\*(C`YYYY\-MM\-DD\*(C'\fR,
and strings in the Header Section are printed using
\&\s-1JSON\s0 <http://json.org/>\-style escape sequences.
Token attribute value strings appear as literals.
.SH "EXAMPLE"
.IX Header "EXAMPLE"
The following is an example file dump produced by \f(CW\*(C`ddc_dump \-\-full \-\-tabs\*(C'\fR for
a small toy file:
.PP
.Vb 10
\& %%$DDC:tokid.begin=0
\& %%$DDC:tokid.end=17
\& %%$DDC:meta.n_=0
\& %%$DDC:meta.file_=test/tiny.xml
\& %%$DDC:meta.scan_=
\& %%$DDC:meta.orig_=
\& %%$DDC:meta.date_=2016\-02\-25
\& %%$DDC:meta.page_=\-1
\& %%$DDC:meta.author=Jurish, Bryan
\& %%$DDC:meta.collection=tiny
\& %%$DDC:meta.textClass=dummy:test\-data
\& %%$DDC:meta.title=DDC test document
\& %%$DDC:index[0]=Token w
\& %%$DDC:index[1]=Pos p
\& %%$DDC:index[2]=Lemma l
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.s[\-1]=0
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.p[\-1]=0
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.file[\-1]=0
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.textarea[\-1]=0
\& This   DT      this
\& is     VBZ     be
\& a      DT      a
\& test   NN      test
\& .      SENT    .
\& 
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.s[0]=5
\& This   DT      this
\& is     VBZ     be
\& only   RB      only
\& a      DT      a
\& test   NN      test
\& .      SENT    .
\& 
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.s[1]=11
\& %%$DDC:BREAK.p[0]=11
\& This   DT      this
\& is     VBZ     be
\& still  RB      still
\& a      DT      a
\& test   NN      test
\& .      SENT    .
.Ve
